#!/bin/sh
# kk-gpu status              one line of json: hybrid, which card draws the desktop, the nvidia
#                            card's power state, the ports wired to it
# kk-gpu set igpu|both|nvidia   which card hyprland draws with (next login):
#   igpu     the integrated one only: best battery; ports wired to nvidia stay dark
#   both     integrated first, nvidia too: every port works; nvidia wakes more often
#   nvidia   everything on the nvidia card: fastest, every port works, the most power
# kk-gpu off | on            take the nvidia card off the bus (no power at all) until `on` or
#                            a reboot. only while the desktop isn't drawing with it.
# kk-gpu run <app> [args]    start one app on the nvidia card (like prime-run)
# kk-gpu hint <addr> <class> a heavy app opened on the integrated card: offer to restart it
set -u
gpu_lua="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/hypr/modules/gpu.lua"
env_file="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/kajukatli/gpu.env"
state="${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/kajukatli"
mkdir -p "$state"

# the nvidia card's pci address (remembered, since it vanishes from sysfs once removed)
pci=""
for d in /sys/bus/pci/devices/*; do
    [ "$(cat "$d/vendor" 2>/dev/null)" = 0x10de ] || continue
    case "$(cat "$d/class" 2>/dev/null)" in 0x03*) pci="${d##*/}"; break ;; esac
done
[ -n "$pci" ] && echo "$pci" > "$state/dgpu-pci"
[ -n "$pci" ] || pci="$(cat "$state/dgpu-pci" 2>/dev/null || true)"

ports=""
for c in /sys/class/drm/card*-*; do
    [ -e "$c/status" ] || continue
    n="${c##*/}"
    case "${n#*-}" in eDP*|LVDS*|DSI*|Writeback*) continue ;; esac
    if [ "$(cat "/sys/class/drm/${n%%-*}/device/vendor" 2>/dev/null)" = 0x10de ]; then
        ports="$ports${ports:+,}\"${n#*-}\""
    fi
done
hybrid=false
[ -e /dev/dri/kk-igpu ] && { [ -e /dev/dri/kk-dgpu ] || [ -n "$pci" ]; } && hybrid=true

hypr_pid() { pgrep -x Hyprland | head -n1; }
live_devs() {
    p="$(hypr_pid)"
    [ -n "$p" ] && tr '\0' '\n' < "/proc/$p/environ" 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/^AQ_DRM_DEVICES=//p'
}
devs_mode() { # AQ_DRM_DEVICES value → igpu|both|nvidia|all
    case "$1" in
        "") echo all ;;
        /dev/dri/kk-dgpu*) echo nvidia ;;
        *kk-dgpu*) echo both ;;
        *) echo igpu ;;
    esac
}

case "${1:-status}" in
    status)
        saved="$(sed -n 's/^AQ_DRM_DEVICES=//p' "$env_file" 2>/dev/null)"
        [ -n "$saved" ] || saved="$(grep -o 'AQ_DRM_DEVICES", *"[^"]*' "$gpu_lua" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/.*"//')"
        mode="$(devs_mode "$saved")"
        now=""
        [ -n "$(hypr_pid)" ] && now="$(devs_mode "$(live_devs)")"
        power=absent
        if [ -n "$pci" ]; then
            if [ -e "/sys/bus/pci/devices/$pci" ]; then
                power="$(cat "/sys/bus/pci/devices/$pci/power/runtime_status" 2>/dev/null || echo active)"
            else
                power=removed
            fi
        fi
        name="$(lspci -s "$pci" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/.*\[\(.*\)\].*/\1/;s/.*: //' | head -n1)"
        dgpu=false; [ -n "$pci" ] && dgpu=true
        # apps on the card right now (yours; the desktop itself not counted)
        hp="$(hypr_pid)"
        users="$(for p in $(fuser /dev/nvidia* 2>/dev/null); do [ "$p" != "$hp" ] && cat "/proc/$p/comm" 2>/dev/null; done | sort -u | sed "s/.*/\"&\"/" | paste -sd, -)"
        printf '{"hybrid":%s,"dgpu":%s,"mode":"%s","running":"%s","power":"%s","runtime":"%s","name":"%s","pci":"%s","dgpuPorts":[%s],"users":[%s]}\n' \
            "$hybrid" "$dgpu" "$mode" "$now" "$power" "$power" "$(printf '%s' "$name" | tr -d '"\\')" "$pci" "$ports" "$users"
        ;;
    set)
        [ "$hybrid" = true ] || { echo "kk-gpu: not a hybrid (two-gpu) machine" >&2; exit 1; }
        extra=""
        case "${2:-}" in
            igpu)   devs="/dev/dri/kk-igpu" ;;
            both)   devs="/dev/dri/kk-igpu:/dev/dri/kk-dgpu" ;;
            nvidia) devs="/dev/dri/kk-dgpu:/dev/dri/kk-igpu"
                    extra="LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=nvidia
__GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia
GBM_BACKEND=nvidia-drm
NVD_BACKEND=direct" ;;
            *) echo "usage: kk-gpu set igpu|both|nvidia" >&2; exit 2 ;;
        esac
        [ -e "/sys/bus/pci/devices/$pci" ] || [ "$2" = igpu ] || { echo "the nvidia card is switched off: kk-gpu on first" >&2; exit 1; }
        mkdir -p "$(dirname "$gpu_lua")" "$(dirname "$env_file")"
        [ -L "$gpu_lua" ] && rm -f "$gpu_lua"
        {
            echo "-- written by kk-gpu (settings → display → graphics). mode: $2"
            echo "hl.env(\"AQ_DRM_DEVICES\", \"$devs\")"
            printf '%s\n' "$extra" | while IFS='=' read -r k v; do
                [ -n "$k" ] && echo "hl.env(\"$k\", \"$v\")"
            done
            [ "$2" = nvidia ] && echo 'hl.config({ cursor = { no_hardware_cursors = 1 } })'
        } > "$gpu_lua"
        # and for kk-session, which exports these before hyprland opens the cards
        { echo "AQ_DRM_DEVICES=$devs"; [ -n "$extra" ] && printf '%s\n' "$extra"; } > "$env_file"
        echo "set to $2. log out and back in to apply."
        ;;
    off)
        [ -n "$pci" ] && [ -e "/sys/bus/pci/devices/$pci" ] || { echo "already off"; exit 0; }
        case "$(live_devs)" in *kk-dgpu*) echo "the desktop itself is drawing with the nvidia card. choose 'integrated only' and log out and back in; then it can go off." >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
        # apps on the card move to the integrated graphics first: each one is closed, then
        # started again (same command, same folder) without the nvidia offload, once the card is off
        moved="$(mktemp -d)"
        hp="$(hypr_pid)"
        n=0
        for p in $(fuser /dev/nvidia* 2>/dev/null | tr -s ' ' '\n' | sort -u); do
            [ -n "$p" ] && [ "$p" != "$hp" ] && [ -r "/proc/$p/cmdline" ] || continue
            [ "$(stat -c %u "/proc/$p")" = "$(id -u)" ] || continue
            cp "/proc/$p/cmdline" "$moved/$p.cmd" 2>/dev/null || continue
            readlink "/proc/$p/cwd" > "$moved/$p.cwd" 2>/dev/null
            cat "/proc/$p/comm" > "$moved/$p.name" 2>/dev/null
            kill "$p" 2>/dev/null && n=$((n + 1))
        done
        i=0
        while [ "$i" -lt 25 ] && [ -n "$(fuser /dev/nvidia* 2>/dev/null | tr -s ' ' '\n' | grep -vx "${hp:-x}" | grep .)" ]; do sleep 0.2; i=$((i + 1)); done
        for f in "$moved"/*.cmd; do [ -e "$f" ] || continue; p="$(basename "$f" .cmd)"; kill -9 "$p" 2>/dev/null || true; done
        # anything left that isn't ours (a system service) keeps the driver busy
        if ! pkexec sh -c "systemctl stop nvidia-persistenced 2>/dev/null; modprobe -r nvidia_drm nvidia_modeset nvidia_uvm nvidia && echo 1 > /sys/bus/pci/devices/$pci/remove"; then
            echo "something of the system's is still using the nvidia card (try: fuser -v /dev/nvidia*); it stays on." >&2
            relaunch=1
        else
            echo "the nvidia card is off (until you switch it on, or reboot)."
        fi
        # the moved apps, again, on the integrated graphics
        names=""
        for f in "$moved"/*.cmd; do
            [ -e "$f" ] || continue
            p="$(basename "$f" .cmd)"
            names="$names $(cat "$moved/$p.name" 2>/dev/null)"
            (
                cd "$(cat "$moved/$p.cwd" 2>/dev/null || echo "$HOME")" 2>/dev/null || cd "$HOME"
                set --
                while IFS= read -r -d '' a; do set -- "$@" "$a"; done < "$f"
                [ "$#" -gt 0 ] && env -u __NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD -u __GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME -u __VK_LAYER_NV_optimus -u DRI_PRIME \
                    setsid -f "$@" >/dev/null 2>&1
            )
        done
        rm -rf "$moved"
        [ "$n" -gt 0 ] && notify-send -a Graphics "Moved to the integrated graphics" "${names# }" 2>/dev/null
        [ "${relaunch:-0}" = 1 ] && exit 1
        exit 0
        ;;
    on)
        [ -n "$pci" ] && [ -e "/sys/bus/pci/devices/$pci" ] && { echo "already on"; exit 0; }
        pkexec sh -c 'echo 1 > /sys/bus/pci/rescan; modprobe nvidia_drm 2>/dev/null; true' && echo "the nvidia card is back."
        ;;
    run)
        shift
        [ "$#" -gt 0 ] || { echo "usage: kk-gpu run <app> [args]" >&2; exit 2; }
        if command -v prime-run >/dev/null; then exec prime-run "$@"; fi
        __NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1 __VK_LAYER_NV_optimus=NVIDIA_only __GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia exec "$@"
        ;;
    hint)
        addr="${2:-}"; cls="${3:-}"
        [ "$hybrid" = true ] && [ -n "$addr" ] || exit 0
        case "$(live_devs)" in /dev/dri/kk-dgpu*) exit 0 ;; esac          # everything is on nvidia already
        pid="$(hyprctl clients -j | jq -r --arg a "$addr" '.[] | select(.address == $a) | .pid' | head -n1)"
        [ -n "$pid" ] && [ "$pid" -gt 0 ] 2>/dev/null || exit 0
        # started on nvidia already?
        tr '\0' '\n' < "/proc/$pid/environ" 2>/dev/null | grep -q '^__NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1' && exit 0
        name="$(cat "/proc/$pid/comm" 2>/dev/null || echo "$cls")"
        case "$cls" in
            steam_app_*)
                notify-send -a Graphics -i nvidia "This game is on the integrated graphics" \
                    "Start Steam from the launcher (it opens on NVIDIA now), or add  kk-gpu run %command%  to the game's launch options." ;;
            *)
                cmd="$(tr '\0' '\n' < "/proc/$pid/cmdline" 2>/dev/null)"
                [ -n "$cmd" ] || exit 0
                act="$(notify-send -a Graphics -i nvidia --action=restart="Restart on NVIDIA" \
                    "$name is on the integrated graphics" "It runs faster on the NVIDIA card. Unsaved work is lost if it restarts.")"
                [ "$act" = restart ] || exit 0
                cwd="$(readlink "/proc/$pid/cwd" 2>/dev/null || echo "$HOME")"
                kill "$pid" 2>/dev/null
                i=0; while kill -0 "$pid" 2>/dev/null && [ "$i" -lt 30 ]; do sleep 0.2; i=$((i + 1)); done
                kill -9 "$pid" 2>/dev/null || true
                # the same command line again, through prime-run
                cd "$cwd" 2>/dev/null || cd "$HOME"
                printf '%s\n' "$cmd" | {
                    set --
                    while IFS= read -r a; do set -- "$@" "$a"; done
                    setsid -f "$0" run "$@" >/dev/null 2>&1
                } ;;
        esac
        ;;
    *) sed -n '2,13p' "$0" | sed 's/^# \{0,1\}//'; exit 2 ;;
esac
